lead: warning: manifest armed for 'epic-z', but this row's role is 'L2 epic-y', which is not that scope. These readers key on an EXACT role_scope, so a role over wider territory does not satisfy them any more than a role over unrelated territory: `fno agents lead done` will refuse, `fno agents lead manifest-path` will exit non-zero without printing a path so the stop hook leaves LEAD_STATE_FILE unset, and the post-compact lead brief will never arrive. Ask an attended shell to re-scope it with `fno agents org promote lead-live --scope epic-z`.
